# Terraform. Neither the provider cache nor state belongs in git: .terraform
# is machine-local, and state stores resource attributes verbatim, including
# values that were never meant to be read. That is precisely why the state
# lives in R2 rather than in a repository, private or otherwise.
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
crash.log
